## Refined intent

**Invariant (locked):** for the same `weight > 0` and `1 ≤ reps ≤ 12`, after the RPE floor clamp, **lower formula RPE ⇒ strictly higher e1RM**.

```text
e1RM(150, 6, 5) > e1RM(150, 6, 6) > e1RM(150, 6, 7)
```

UI `Math.round` must preserve that: **214 > 205 > 197**. Display must not be 150 for @5.

The 25% cap **violates** the invariant (maps @5 and @6 to 200). A post-formula `min(e1RM, weight / 0.75)` is the same function and also equalizes. **Drop the cap.** Do not invent an RPE-dependent cap or a Helms table.

`reps > 12 → weight` stays the high-rep reliability guard. Denom `<= 0.1` stays as a zero-division guard (does not fire for `reps ≤ 12` and `formula_rpe ≥ 5`).

### Locked decisions

| Decision | Verdict | Why |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| Formula family | **Keep** linear decay `e1RM = weight / (1 - 0.03 * (10 - formula_rpe + reps - 1))` | One canonical formula; no Helms/Brzycki |
| RPE floor | **Keep** `E1RM_RPE_FLOOR = 5.0` from the floor rule | Logged 5 must run; `< 5` clamps input only |
| Missing RPE / `reps > 12` | **Keep** return `weight` | Empty LOG RPE ≠ RPE 5 |
| 25% metabolic drop cap | **Drop** in `calculate_e1rm` / `calculateE1RM` **and** `calculateWeightFromE1RM` | Cap flattens 150×6 @5 and @6 to 200; also flattens all RPE for 10-rep sets (100×10 @5/@6/@8 all 133.33 under the cap) |
| Replacement cap constant | **None** | Any fixed drop cap equalizes every RPE whose uncapped drop exceeds it |
| Ranking | **Strict** on formula RPE: `formula_rpe_lo < formula_rpe_hi` ⇒ `e1RM_lo > e1RM_hi` | Product: easier set at the same load ⇒ higher estimated max |
| Floor clamp vs ranking | `@4 == @5` is required (same formula RPE). `@5 > @6` is required (different formula RPE) | Do not “fix” ranking by unclamping RPE 4 |
| `MATH_VERSION` | **Bump** `linear-decay-v2` → **`linear-decay-v3`** | v2’s published contract is 150×6@5 → 200 (capped). New outputs. Sync 409 |
| Persist athlete RPE | **Unchanged** | Clamp is formula-input only |
| LOG RPE input | **Executed** (`set.executedRpe`) | Already wired in `ExerciseCard` |
| `RPE_CHART` | **Do not extend** | Not on the e1RM path |

### Formula (locked)

```text
if weight <= 0 or reps <= 0: return 0
if reps > 12: return weight
if rpe <= 0: return weight
formula_rpe = rpe if rpe >= 5.0 else 5.0
effective_drop = 0.03 * (10 - formula_rpe + reps - 1)   # NO min(..., 0.25)
denom = 1.0 - effective_drop
if denom <= 0.1: return weight
return round(weight / denom, 2)
```

Delete `if effective_drop_pct > 0.25: effective_drop_pct = 0.25` in Python and TypeScript (including the inverse).

### Worked numbers (contract)

Uncapped: `effective_drop = 0.03 * (10 - formula_rpe + reps - 1)`. Round 2 dp.

| weight | reps | logged RPE | formula RPE | e1RM | UI `Math.round` | note |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | ---: | ---: | :--- |
| 150 | 6 | 5.0 | 5.0 | **214.29** | **214** | user case; **not** 150, **not** 200 |
| 150 | 6 | 6.0 | 6.0 | **205.48** | **205** | @5 > @6 |
| 150 | 6 | 7.0 | 7.0 | **197.37** | **197** | @6 > @7 |
| 150 | 6 | 5.5 | 5.5 | **209.79** | **210** | between @5 and @6 |
| 150 | 6 | 4.0 | 5.0 | **214.29** | **214** | == @5 (floor) |
| 150 | 6 | 0 / null | — | **150.00** | **150** | missing RPE |
| 100 | 5 | 5.5 | 5.5 | **134.23** | — | v2 was 133.33 **because of the cap** (drop 0.255) |
| 100 | 10 | 8.0 | 8.0 | **149.25** | — | v1/v2 vector 133.33 was the cap; must change |
| 100 | 3 | 5.0 | 5.0 | **126.58** | — | unchanged (drop 0.21 < 0.25) |
| 100 | 3 | 5.5 | 5.5 | **124.22** | — | unchanged; 5.5 not clamped |
| 100 | 5 | 9.0 | 9.0 | 117.65 | — | unchanged |
| 100 | 1 | 10.0 | 10.0 | 100.00 | — | unchanged |

INOL follows e1RM. 150×6@5: `intensity_pct: 70`, `inol: 0.2`. 150×6@6: `73` / `0.22`. 150×6@7: `76` / `0.25`. 100×5@5.5: `e1rm: 134.23`, `intensity_pct: 74.5`, `inol: 0.2`. 100×10@8: `e1rm: 149.25`, `intensity_pct: 67`, `inol: 0.3`.

